# Technical stack

`package.json` holds the exact versions. Never upgrade a major version as a side effect of another
change; a major upgrade is its own PR.

| Area            | Choice                                                                 | Where                                                       |
| --------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- |
| Framework       | Next.js 15, App Router                                                 | `src/app/`, `src/middleware.ts`                             |
| UI              | React 19, Tailwind CSS 4, Radix UI primitives                          | `src/components/ui/`, `src/styles/`                         |
| Language        | TypeScript 5.9, `strict`                                               | `tsconfig.json`; alias `@/*` → `src/*`                      |
| Database        | PostgreSQL 16 through Prisma 6                                         | `prisma/schema.prisma`; client in `src/lib/db/prisma.ts`    |
| Validation      | Zod 4, at the boundary only                                            | route handlers, adapters                                    |
| Client state    | Zustand 5 for client state, TanStack Query 5 for server state          | stores and hooks                                            |
| Auth            | Auth.js (`next-auth` 5 beta), JWT sessions, personal API keys          | `src/lib/auth/`, `src/lib/api/authenticate.ts`              |
| i18n            | next-intl 4; served locales `en` and `fr`                              | `src/i18n/`, `src/messages/<locale>/`                       |
| Logging         | pino, Sentry                                                           | `src/lib/logger.ts`, `sentry.*.config.ts`                   |
| Unit tests      | Vitest 3, Testing Library, jsdom; tests next to the code (`*.test.ts`) | `vitest.config.ts`, shared test kit in `src/test/`          |
| End-to-end      | Playwright in Docker, run by the pre-push hook (no CI job)             | `e2e/`, `docker-compose.e2e.yml`, `scripts/e2e-pre-push.sh` |
| Mutation        | StrykerJS on `src/modules/*/domain/**`, nightly and on PRs, advisory   | `stryker.config.mjs`, `.github/workflows/mutation.yml`      |
| Lint and format | ESLint 9 flat config (`eslint.config.mjs`), Prettier 3              | `.lintstagedrc.cjs` runs both on commit                     |
| Tooling         | pnpm 10 (`packageManager`), Node 22 in CI, Husky hooks                 | `.github/workflows/`, `.husky/`                             |

## Rules

- **Server code stays on the server.** Prisma, secrets and provider keys never reach a client
  component, a hook or a store. When the `server-only` package lands
  (`docs/adr/0007-architecture-enforcement-in-stages.md`), every such module imports it.
- **One adapter per external provider.** Scryfall, Commander Spellbook, Anthropic and OpenAI,
  EDHREC, MTGTop8 and each deck-import site are reached through their own adapter, which turns the
  provider's wire format into domain types
  (`docs/adr/0004-anti-corruption-layers-for-external-providers.md`). Domain code never imports a
  provider type such as `ScryfallCard`.
- **Route handlers stay route handlers.** Do not convert them to Server Actions.
- **Planned tooling is not there yet.** The ESLint flat config, size limits,
  `eslint-plugin-jsdoc`, MSW, Knip and Stryker are planned
  (`docs/engineering/quality-gate.md`, "Planned gates"). Do not write code or docs that assume
  they exist.
- **A new dependency needs a reason.** Say in the PR why no existing package or a few lines of
  code would do. CI blocks on a high-severity `pnpm audit --prod` finding.
